locales-offered-help = The realm's cut of what this build speaks. Unchecking all offers everything; a realm cannot offer a tongue the build does not carry.
locales-default = Default language
locales-default-help = What answers when neither the request's ui_locales nor the browser's list names an offered tongue.
locales-default-first = the first offered
locale-en = English
locale-fr = French
policy-min-length = Minimum length
policy-min-length-help = The floor. Length beats complexity: prefer raising this over class counts.
policy-max-length = Maximum length
policy-max-length-help = A ceiling for pathological inputs; the hasher caps cost anyway. Leave unset unless something downstream demands one.
policy-min-digits = Digits
policy-min-digits-help = How many digits a password must carry.
policy-min-upper = Upper case
policy-min-upper-help = How many upper case letters a password must carry.
policy-min-lower = Lower case
policy-min-lower-help = How many lower case letters a password must carry.
policy-min-special = Special characters
policy-min-special-help = How many characters outside letters and digits a password must carry.
policy-expiry = Expires after, days
policy-expiry-help = Forces a change this many days after it was set. Unset never expires; forced rotation mostly breeds suffixes.
policy-history = History compared
policy-history-help = A new password is refused when it matches this many previous ones.
policy-not-email = Not the email address
policy-not-email-help = Refuses a password equal to the account's own address.
policy-not-username = Not the username
policy-not-username-help = Refuses a password equal to the account's own username.
policy-not-birthdate = Not the birth date
policy-not-birthdate-help = Refuses a password equal to the account's stored birth date.
policy-regex = Pattern
policy-regex-help = A regular expression every new password must match. Empty imposes none.
policy-blacklist = Refused words
policy-blacklist-help = Passwords containing any of these are refused, case-insensitively: the company name, the product, the city.
policy-blacklist-hint = one per line
policy-hashing-line = Stored with Argon2id: { $memory } KiB, { $passes } passes, { $lanes } lane(s).
policy-hashing-help = What a stored password costs to compute, the server's own OWASP baseline. Set beside the deployment, not per save; shown so an operator knows what is in force.
flows-binding = Browser flow
flows-binding-help = Which top-level flow answers /authorize when the client binds none of its own. The built default is the flow aliased browser.
flows-binding-default = the built default (browser)
flows-binding-subject = browser flow binding
otp-title = One-time codes
otp-title-help = What a newly enrolled authenticator app is set up with. A credential keeps the shape it was minted with, so changes reshape the next enrolment and never break codes already in someone's app. The window applies to every login now.
otp-digits = Digits
otp-digits-help = How many digits a code shows. Six is what every app expects.
otp-period = Period, seconds
otp-period-help = How long one code lives. Thirty is the ecosystem's clock.
otp-algorithm = Digest
otp-algorithm-help = SHA1 is the one digest every authenticator app implements; a stronger one here enrols cleanly in apps that then generate codes that never match. Change only for a controlled fleet.
otp-window = Drift window
otp-window-help = How many steps either side of now a code is still accepted, at every login. Each step widens acceptance by one period each way.
webauthn-title = Passkeys
webauthn-title-help = How this realm presents itself to a browser's key ceremony. Keys are scoped to the party they were enrolled against; the security posture itself is fixed by the verifier.
webauthn-rp-name = Shown name
webauthn-rp-name-help = What the browser's dialog names during enrolment and sign-in. Empty shows the origin's host.
webauthn-subdomains = Apex answers for subdomains
webauthn-subdomains-help = A key enrolled at example.com also answers on app.example.com. Off, every host stands alone.
webauthn-fixed-line = Fixed by the verifier: user verification required, no attestation collected. That is the passkey contract, not a setting.
group-default = Every new account joins this group
group-default-help = Birthright membership: accounts created after the mark land here at creation, whichever door made them, an administrator, a federation, a SCIM push. Unmarking stops the intake and touches nobody already inside.
group-default-chip = default
