## The writing doors of the bonus screens: roles, scopes, organizations,
## policies, relations, flow steps, governance, client roles, sub-groups.
role-new = New role
role-name-help = How grants and tokens spell it. Renaming keeps every grant; the identifier underneath never changes.
role-delete = Delete this role
role-delete-lede = Refused while anyone still holds it. Grants go first, then the role.
scope-new = New scope
scope-name-help = What clients ask for, word for word. Choose it like an API name.
scope-sentence = Consent sentence
scope-sentence-help = The line a person reads on the consent screen when a client asks for this scope.
scope-attach-mapper = Attach a mapper
scope-delete = Delete this scope
org-new = New organization
org-claim = Claim a domain
org-claim-domain = Domain
org-claim-help = Claiming answers with a TXT record to publish. The claim proves nothing until checked.
org-domain-check = Check
org-challenge-lede = Publish this record in the domain's DNS, then check. The check records your word that the record is up; nothing probes the DNS for you.
org-delete = Delete this organization
org-delete-lede = Members lose a label, not an entitlement. Domains claimed by it go with it.
authz-protect = Protect a client
authz-new-policy = New policy
authz-new-resource = New resource
authz-write-relation = Write a relation
authz-palette = Evaluator palette
authz-palette-sub = what each policy type weighs
authz-palette-lede = The evaluators ship in the build. A policy names one and carries its terms; the decision point folds their answers under the resource's strategy.
authz-enforcement = Enforcement
authz-enforcement-help = Enforcing refuses what no policy allows. Permissive decides but lets everything pass, for reading the would-be refusals first. Disabled stands aside.
authz-strategy = Decision strategy
authz-strategy-help = How several answers fold into one: any yes carries it, all must agree, or the majority decides.
authz-evaluator = Policy type
authz-evaluator-help = Which evaluator reads this policy. The type fixes what the terms mean.
authz-terms = Terms
authz-terms-help = One name per line. What they name depends on the type: roles for a role policy, groups for a group policy.
authz-resource-type = Type
authz-resource-type-help = A word of your own that groups kindred resources, like document or account.
authz-resource-uris = URIs
authz-resource-uris-help = The paths this resource stands for, one per line.
authz-resource-owner = Owner
authz-subject-type = Subject type
authz-subject-id = Subject
authz-relation-name = Relation
authz-relation-help = The verb between subject and object, like owner or editor. The relationship walk follows these edges.
authz-object-type = Object type
authz-object-id = Object
authz-relation-lede = A tuple written here is standing fact, not policy: subject, relation, object. There is no listing yet; the simulator is how a written edge is read back.
authz-write = Write
authz-erase = Erase
authz-tuple-kept = Written. The edge holds until erased.
authz-tuple-test = Read it back with the decision simulator: ask as the subject about the object.
authz-family-who = who you are
authz-family-what = what is true of you
authz-family-owns = how things relate
authz-family-narrows = narrows when
authz-family-composes = composes others
flow-add-step = Add a step
flow-step-what = Authenticator
flow-step-what-help = Which challenge this step puts to the person. The catalogue is the build's own; nothing arrives at runtime.
flow-requirement-help = Required must pass. Alternatives satisfy the stage together: any one is enough. Disabled never runs.
flow-add-note = The step lands after the last one; reorder by editing priorities.
flow-remove-step = Remove this step
rule-new = New rule
rule-converge = Converge now
rule-converge-help = Walks every enabled rule at once instead of waiting for the sweeper's next pass.
rule-mode-attribute = By attribute
rule-mode-expr = By expression
rule-mode-expr-help = A small predicate over the person's attributes. Absence is inequality: a missing attribute fails an equals and passes a not-equals.
rule-attribute = Attribute
rule-value = Value
rule-expr = Expression
rule-roles = Roles granted
rule-roles-help = Role identifiers, comma separated. What a rule grants, only that rule revokes, when its condition stops holding.
rule-boundary = Rules only ever revoke what they granted.
rule-pause = Pause
rule-enable = Enable
iga-grant-role = Role
iga-grant-until = Until
iga-grant-until-help = An RFC 3339 instant. The grant dies on its own at that time; empty grants for good.
iga-grant-give = Grant
client-tab-roles = Roles
